    {
      "id": "the-two-noble-kinsmen/sceneIII_38.4/p@92828",
      "type": "passage",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "For I’ll cut my green coat a foot above my knee,\nAnd I’ll clip my yellow locks an inch below mine eye.\nHey nonny, nonny, nonny.\nHe’s buy me a white cut, forth for to ride,\nAnd I’ll go seek him through the world that is so wide.\nHey nonny, nonny, nonny.\nO, for a prick now, like a nightingale,\nTo put my breast against. I shall sleep like a top else.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
